requested_changes.body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The training statistics are not aggregated across all distributed processes before being logged. Currently, each process logs its local statistics, but since `wandb` is only active on rank 0, only the statistics from rank 0's data shard are being recorded. This can lead to noisy and unrepresentative metrics. The statistics should be averaged across all ranks before logging.

```suggestion
            stats = out["stats"]
            for stat_tensor in stats.values():
                if torch.is_tensor(stat_tensor):
                    torch.distributed.all_reduce(stat_tensor, op=torch.distributed.ReduceOp.AVG)

            stats = {k: float(v) for k, v in stats.items()}
            stats = {f"train/{key}": value for key, value in stats.items()}
            wandb.log(stats, step=self.global_step)
```

